Extrema_GenExtPS: the grid of a B-spline range of very many knot spans
holds at most 1001 parameters in a direction, evenly spaced (mitcad#235).

The projection of a point onto a B-spline surface (GeomAPI_ProjectPointOnSurf,
the boolean's projector of each face in IntTools_Context, ShapeAnalysis'
ValueOfUV in the face merge) puts its grid at the degree's number of
parameters in each knot span, and every projection computes the distances
to all of the grid's nodes, edges and cells. On a thread's face running 25
turns (4000 knot spans along the helix, 12000 grid rows) one projection
cost about 500000 of each, the union of a part with such a thread insert
spent most of its 13 s in them, and each face's grid held 100 MB in every
thread's context (7.5 GB for that union).

A direction of more than 1001 such parameters is now sampled at 1001
parameters evenly over the range, as many as Adaptor3d_TopolTool samples a
B-spline at most (BSplSamplePnts); a range of fewer is unchanged.

--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_GenExtPS.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_GenExtPS.cxx
@@ -361,6 +361,22 @@
   {
     return;
   }
+  // A range of very many knot spans (a thread's face running tens of turns,
+  // its helices interpolated at a hundred points a turn: 10000 parameters)
+  // is sampled evenly at as many points as Adaptor3d_TopolTool samples a
+  // B-spline at most: every projection computes the distances to all nodes,
+  // edges and cells of the grid (mitcad#235).
+  constexpr int THE_MAX_PARAMS = 1001;
+  if (nbPar > THE_MAX_PARAMS)
+  {
+    theParams = new NCollection_HArray1<double>(1, THE_MAX_PARAMS);
+    for (i = 0; i < THE_MAX_PARAMS; i++)
+    {
+      theParams->SetValue(i + 1,
+                          theParMin + (theParMax - theParMin) * i / (THE_MAX_PARAMS - 1));
+    }
+    return;
+  }
   theParams = new NCollection_HArray1<double>(1, nbPar);
   for (i = 0; i < nbPar; i++)
   {
